{"duration_api_ms":34280,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8563b58f-9b22-451c-92e0-10949baec312","total_cost_usd":0.29003140000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":20,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33579,"cache_read_input_tokens":254882,"output_tokens":3554,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":200},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":33579},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":20,"outputTokens":3554,"cacheReadInputTokens":254882,"cacheCreationInputTokens":33579,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.29003140000000005,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":200,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":10,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Patterns passed with `--and` now get the same path-separator error as the main pattern. Before, something like `fd foo --and one/two` just returned nothing, because patterns are matched against file names and a name never contains `/`. All tests pass (139 unit, 111 integration).\n\n**What changed** (`src/main.rs`):\n- `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now checks the main pattern and then each `--and` pattern, and errors on the first one that contains a separator.\n- I moved the check itself into a helper, `pattern_looks_like_a_path`. The rule is the same as before: any `/` counts, and on Windows a `\\` counts only if the pattern is a real directory. The `--full-path` exemption still applies to all patterns.\n- The error message is unchanged and names whichever pattern triggered it.\n\n**Tests and changelog:**\n- New test `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected` in `tests/tests.rs`. It covers a single `--and` pattern with `/`, a bad pattern after a valid `--and`, and confirms `--full-path` still lets `--and one/two` through.\n- Added an entry under Unreleased → Bugfixes in `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\nTwo things to know:\n- When it's an `--and` pattern that triggers the error, part of the message is less useful: it suggests `fd . '<pattern>'`, which drops the main pattern. The `--full-path` suggestion still makes sense. I kept one message for simplicity; I can tailor the wording for `--and` if you want.\n- I couldn't run `cargo fmt` because rustfmt isn't installed here, so formatting wasn't checked by the tool. I formatted the changed lines by hand to match. Clippy's warnings are all in `tests/tests.rs` and were there before this change; none come from what I touched.\n\nNothing is committed yet.","ttft_ms":2098,"type":"result","duration_ms":95119,"uuid":"266b9934-bbb4-4801-bc60-e7083996c708","ttft_stream_ms":892,"time_to_request_ms":92,"first_content_frame_ms":892,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
